# Attributes for the website folder only. The repository's own .gitattributes
# (* text=auto) lets Git decide what is text by looking for NUL bytes, and
# with core.autocrlf a file it takes for text is rewritten with the system's
# line endings at checkout.
#
# That is wrong for two kinds of file here:
#
# - A PDF can be free of NUL bytes (samples/files/horary-reading-v1.pdf is),
#   so Git takes it for text and a Windows checkout would insert carriage
#   returns into it. The site's binary types are therefore declared, so that
#   none of them depends on detection.
# - The sample reports offered as Markdown downloads are served "as AstroCast
#   wrote it", mixed line endings included. They are stored byte for byte.
#
# The Markdown sources in samples-src/ are ordinary text: Git stores them
# with LF endings, and tools/Build-Samples.ps1 reads either.
*.pdf   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
AstroCast/samples/files/*.md -text
